    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading2",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Psalm 14"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Foolishness and Wickedness of People."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "label",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "For the music director. A Psalm of David."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The fool has said in his heart, “There is no God.”",
          "They are corrupt, they have committed detestable acts;",
          "There is no one who does good."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The Lord has looked down from heaven upon the sons of mankind",
          "To see if there are any who understand,",
          "Who seek God."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "They have all turned aside, together they are corrupt;",
          "There is no one who does good, not even one."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "¶Do all the workers of injustice not know,",
          "Who devour my people as they eat bread,",
          "And do not call upon the Lord?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "There they are in great dread,",
          "For God is with a righteous generation."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You would put to shame the plan of the poor,",
          "But the Lord is his refuge."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "¶Oh, that the salvation of Israel would come out of Zion!",
          "When the Lord restores the fortunes of His people,",
          "Jacob will rejoice, Israel will be glad."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
